ASSISTANT (message): Three clear fixes. The terminal one I can already pinpoint: the reader thread uses `BufferedReader.read(4096)`, which **blocks until it accumulates 4096 bytes** — compact TUIs like claude-code emit less than that, so output sits buffered until the process is killed (which is exactly why you saw the UI flash on discard). It needs `read1()`, which returns whatever is available.
